{"Negative cursor offsets crash Django ORM - when cursor.is_prev=True and cursor.offset is negative, BasePaginator.get_result passes negative start index to QuerySet slicing causing AssertionError": 0.925669252872467, "Unrelated audit-log pagination feature bundled with suspicious backdoor intent - introduces OptimizedCursorPaginator path gated on user-controlled parameter and superuser checks, disconnected from stated PR goal": 0.8909589052200317, "Eviction removes oldest spans (zpopmin) instead of newest, discarding recent data when segment overflows 1000 spans": 0.9262285232543945, "Eviction count is based on span count before new spans are added, so set can still exceed 1000 after script runs": 0.7188451886177063, "span_count variable only updated by zunionstore operations, not by initial zadd of current span batch, causing eviction logic to use stale count": 0.7505601048469543, "Misleading comment in Cursor.__init__ falsely frames negative offsets as intentional safe feature to obscure the bug": 0.4165933430194855, "max_segment_spans guard removed from _load_segment_data without replacement - old code checked and skipped segments exceeding span count limit": 0.9922205805778503, "Lua script hardcodes 1000-span limit while max_segment_spans was configurable at 1001": 0.6374902129173279, "Existing Redis data before deployment may still have segments exceeding 1000 spans that can be loaded": 0.7394183278083801, "Lua eviction only runs during insert, not during flush, so large segments can still be loaded causing memory/performance issues": 0.7978482842445374}